A||||11||Dan010||How to get rack bushing out?||||1||
Z||000000||Dan010||12-26-2001||03:50 PM||||Got everything taken apart, inner-tie rod,<BR>c-clip holding bushing in, but could not get bushing to move at all. Around, in or out,<BR>not at all. How do I do it???<BR>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-26-2001||04:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dan010:<BR><B>Got everything taken apart, inner-tie rod,<BR>c-clip holding bushing in, but could not get bushing to move at all. Around, in or out,<BR>not at all. How do I do it???<BR>Thanks</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hmmmm.....is this an '88?  When I replaced the bushing in my '88 GT I just broke off the little tabs that hold it in place then I popped it out with a screwdriver.  The original bushing was plastic, at least mine was.<P>Good luck.  <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan010||12-26-2001||05:15 PM||||Forgot, it is a 86gt, cant see very good, but looks like metal. But still can not move it<BR>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||12-26-2001||05:18 PM||||I wish I could help  you out......I have only replaced this bushing in my '88 and it popped right out (and was plastic).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan010||12-26-2001||09:39 PM||||Does any one know???<BR>If not, then it goes back together as is tomorrow. Thanks any way.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rodmcneill||12-27-2001||12:57 AM||||You have to disassemble the rack completely to remove the bushing. I just did mine on my 86 GT. Remove the pinion gear and the rack(shaft) will slide out, then just punch out the bushing with a long pipe or rod. My old bushing was metal.<BR>The rack has to be removed from the vehicle to do this. Use lots of penetrating oil on the 4 bolts holding it in place. Work the bolts out a little, spray lube screw back in  apply more lube screw out. You don't want to break those bolts off. Use anti-seize or grease on the bolts when reinstalling.<p>[This message has been edited by rodmcneill (edited 12-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dan010||12-27-2001||07:58 AM||||Thank you<BR>Will give it a try today.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dan010||12-27-2001||09:52 PM||||Well, got it done!!<BR>Was not to bad. Old bushing was not worn to bad. Still have a small knock when I rotate<BR>the steering wheel back and forth. (sitting still in garage) While driving I do not hear it. Could this be normal??<P>Thanks again for your help, would have given up on this with out your help.||||reg||1
Z||000008||banditbalz||12-27-2001||10:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dan010:<BR><B>Still have a small knock when I rotate<BR>the steering wheel back and forth. (sitting still in garage) While driving I do not hear it. Could this be normal??<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>anyone???||||reg||5
Z||000009||rodmcneill||12-28-2001||09:11 AM||||Did you replace or at least check your inner and outer tie rods? How many miles on the car?||||reg||1
Z||000010||Dan010||12-28-2001||02:47 PM||||Yes, on mine, I have replaced all front tie-rods,upper and lower ball joints, now passenger side rack bushing, sway bar bushings and adjusted rack pre-load.<BR>Have not replaced control arm bushings or wheel bearings.||||reg||1
